  {
    "id": "20039a87a25f6734ea92692b01d35974a61981e6",
    "individual_note": false,
    "resolvable": true,
    "resolved": true,
    "notes": [
      {
        "id": 3956488892,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "**Blocking: accepting the record drops every other ability of a multi-ability object**\n\n**Location.** `objsave_replace_special_ability()`, `src/obj/objsave.c:123-142`; the writers at `objsave.c:542`, `:3499` and `:4534`.\n\n**Defect.** The three writers store only the first ability of the list (`specab = obj->special_abilities;`, no loop). The loader frees the whole list (line 129) and installs that one record. On master a first record with no command word is rejected, so a prototype-backed object keeps the full list `read_object()` copied from its prototype. This change accepts the record, and the rest of the list is freed.\n\nA first ability that has a command word already loses the rest on master. No multi-ability prototype in the dev world files has one first, so today nothing is truncated; after this change all of them are:\n\n| Object | Abilities | After load |\n| -- | -- | -- |\n| #1213 a black longsword | Bane, Flaming Burst (`ignitus`) | Bane; `utter ignitus` does nothing |\n| #1244 black scythe | Bane, Keen | Bane |\n| #20621 cat-o'-nine-tails | Keen, Wounding | Keen |\n\nFourteen more prototypes carry two `SPECAB_NONE` placeholder records, with no effect. Every saved copy loads this way from the first login after the deploy: player rows, house rows, pet rows, sheath contents and rent files all go through this function. The row never held the other abilities, so nothing stored is destroyed, and a corrected loader brings them back from the prototype.\n\nThe description's \"logged `Invalid SpAb record` and dropped the ability\" is true for an object with no prototype. A prototype-backed object kept its prototype's abilities, which is why accepting the record changes more than the description says.\n\n**Repro.** A prototype with the two records of #1244 (`3 30 48 1 20 0 0`, `15 30 1 0 0 0 0`), `read_object()`, then `test_objsave_save_obj_record()` + `objsave_parse_objects()` and `objsave_save_obj_record_db()` + `objsave_parse_objects_db()`, counting the abilities before and after. Run at `ab7a35b84` and again with `objsave.c` from `c8a28d892`, database tests on:\n\n```\nsaved line: SpAb: 3 30 48 1 20 0 0\nobjsave.c of c8a28d892: file loader 2 -> 2, player rows 2 -> 2  (SYSERR logged, prototype list kept)\nab7a35b84:              file loader 2 -> 1, player rows 2 -> 1  (Keen gone)\n```\n\n**Fix.** Keep the list and let the record replace one ability, not all of them:\n\n```c\n  /* The writers store the first ability only. It replaces the ability of its\n   * kind, or else the first one, and the rest of the list stays. */\n  for (ability = obj->special_abilities; ability != NULL; ability = ability->next)\n    if (ability->ability == values[0])\n      break;\n  if (ability == NULL)\n    ability = obj->special_abilities;\n  if (ability == NULL)\n  {\n    CREATE(ability, struct obj_special_ability, 1);\n    obj->special_abilities = ability;\n  }\n  else if (ability->command_word != NULL)\n    free(ability->command_word);\n  ability->ability = values[0];\n  /* level, activation_method and value[0..3] as now */\n  ability->command_word = fields == 8 ? strdup(command) : NULL;\n```\n\nThe `free_obj_special_abilities()` call, `ability->next = NULL` and the list assignment go. Match by kind, not by position: the first ability is not a stable place. `db.c:4151` prepends each `C` record and `genobj.c:350` writes the list in order, so an OLC save of the zone reverses the records, and a different ability is first after the next boot.\n\nTested on `ab7a35b84` with that change: the probe gives 2 -> 2 through both loaders, the three tests of this merge request pass, and the whole `./cutest` passes with the database tests on.\n\nAdd the probe as a test: the two-ability prototype round trip through the file loader and the player-row loader, asserting both abilities.\n\n**Older than this merge request, still open after the fix.** The writers save one ability. A change to any other ability of an instance is not persisted (the weapon-oil upgrade loop at `act.item.c:6123` can upgrade one that is not first), and an object with no prototype keeps only its first. Saving the whole list needs one line per ability and a way to tell today's one-line rows from new ones, so it is its own work item.",
