      {
        "id": 3957440466,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Fixed in `1d904677a`, with the fix as proposed: the record replaces the ability of its kind, or else the first one, and the rest of the list stays. `free_obj_special_abilities()`, `ability->next = NULL` and the list assignment are gone.\n\nI checked the two choices in it against the code that changes an object's list before taking them:\n\n- By kind first: confirmed, `parse_object()` puts each `C` record in front and `save_objects()` writes the list in order, so the abilities change places at the boot after a zone save.\n- The first ability as the fallback, not a new node in front: a weapon oil turns Flaming into Flaming Burst on the object alone, so the saved kind is one the prototype does not have and must take the old one's place.\n\nTest: `Test_object_special_ability_record_keeps_the_rest_of_the_prototype_list`. It uses #1213 (Bane, Flaming Burst on `ignitus`) and not #1244, so that the second ability's command word is checked too. The saved Bane carries a bane race of its own, so the test also fails if the record is passed over. It covers:\n\n1. the round trip through the file loader, and through the player-row loader when the database tests are on, with both abilities compared;\n2. the same file loaded with the prototype's list the other way round;\n3. a first ability that has a command word, which lost the rest on master too;\n4. an ability of a kind the prototype does not have.\n\nIt fails on the loader of `ab7a35b84` at the first of these, on the fix without the match by kind at the second, and on the fix with an unmatched ability put in front at the fourth.\n\nVerification on `1d904677a`: `make -j16 test` 2039 pass; `./cutest` with the database tests on, on a freshly loaded `master_schema.sql` database, 2038 of 2039 (the #18 test); `run.py --base gitlab/master` 33 of 33 jobs (357 s).\n\nThe description now says what a rejected record did to a prototype-backed object, and the plan has the review's record (`c62c01124`).\n\n**The writers.** Filed as #28, with two cases run on `1d904677a` through the file writer and loader: an emptied list comes back as the prototype's two abilities (0 saved, 2 loaded), and a second ability changed from level 12 to 20 loads as 12.\n\n**Seen while tracing, unrelated to the loader.** `downgrade_item()` and `do_applyoil()` drop ability lists without freeing them, and the preview branch of `do_downgrade()` never extracts its preview object. Filed as #29.",
