      {
        "id": 3956495652,
        "type": null,
        "body": "**Review of `ab7a35b84`: one finding, blocking**\n\n1. Accepting the seven-number record frees the rest of a multi-ability object's list, so #1213, #1244 and #20621 load with their first ability only. Thread on `src/obj/objsave.c:123`, with the repro and a tested fix.\n\nReproduced from the description, on a scratch build with a disposable `mariadb:10.11` loaded from `sql/master_schema.sql`:\n\n- With `objsave.c` from `c8a28d892`, the round-trip test fails and the file, player-row and pet-row loaders each log the rejected record. At `ab7a35b84` it passes with the database tests on.\n- With `spec_abilities.c` from `c8a28d892`, the `utter` test kills the process.\n- Every reader of `command_word` handles NULL. The one unguarded `strcmp()`, in `process_item_abilities()`, has no caller that passes a command word, as the plan says.\n- The pet save fingerprint hashes a NULL word and an empty word alike, so the change of representation does not force a pet resave.\n- `utter` reaches the flame-blade branch of `process_weapon_abilities()` with a NULL victim and returns.\n\nNo other findings.",
